{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Pr7JorUwh3xGWdKDiH8Hbg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge on edge cases. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI code generation, and verifies output parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). Human-authored SRDs drive AI code generation via mage-claude-orchestrator. Go implementations live in `cmd/`, shared infrastructure in `pkg/` (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil). Differential testing compares Go and Homebrew GNU binaries byte-for-byte.\n\n**Current State**: All pkg/ infrastructure is implemented. Implemented cmd/ utilities: sponge, du, true, false, yes, basename, dirname, tee, head, seq, wc. Run 44 is active on branch `generation-run44`. Releases 00.0 through 03.0 are complete or have no ready requirements remaining.\n\n**Current Release**: Release 03.1 (system information: uname, arch, nproc, hostname, hostid) is the earliest release with all requirements in `ready` state.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 03.1 contains 5 trivial system information utilities. Ordered by complexity: arch (7 reqs), hostid (7 reqs), hostname (7 reqs), nproc (10 reqs), uname (16 reqs). All have `ready` status on every requirement. Dependencies are minimal -- just pkg/sys for SIGPIPE handling.\n\nWith a 4-task limit and 4 sub-requirements per task, I propose core implementation tasks (R1/R2 groups) for the 4 simplest utilities. Testing/edge-case tasks (R3+ groups) follow in the next batch per P2 (split implementation and tests) and P8 (implementation before tests).\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nWeights assumed default 1 per requirement (cannot read requirements.yaml per constraints).\n\n- Task 0: srd045-arch R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4\n- Task 1: srd048-hostid R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4\n- Task 2: srd047-hostname R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R2.1 (w=1) + R2.2 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4\n- Task 3: srd046-nproc R1.1 (w=1) + R1.2 (w=1) + R1.3 (w=1) + R1.4 (w=1) = 4 ≤ 4\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/arch: core implementation and error handling (srd045-arch R1.1-R1.2, R2.1-R2.2)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd045-arch.yaml (full SRD for arch)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler usage and existing syscall wrappers)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (shared protocols and import constraints)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/arch/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: arch utility -- prints machine hardware name to stdout\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd045-arch R1.1 -- print the machine hardware name to stdout\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd045-arch R1.2 -- output formatting and newline termination\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd045-arch R2.1 -- --help flag prints usage to stdout and exits 0\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd045-arch R2.2 -- --version flag prints version to stdout and exits 0\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at start of main per shared protocol\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Per architecture, cmd/ packages must not import golang.org/x/sys directly -- route platform syscalls through pkg/sys or use Go standard library\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build -o bin/arch ./cmd/arch/ succeeds without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/arch/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"bin/arch prints the machine hardwa